{"canonical_record":{"canonical_payload_sha256":"c54ad18c03212f0d3e8bb66cc72f9b92a85a995938a9a4c1c107333d7deef07d","full_review_record_id":"fullrev_05bb96b723e210b41f5477e75b558f842b919fbc9f68c4e8eac610f891016847","overall_assessment":"The paper presents a technical framework for image generation using public datasets. The supplied evidence is insufficient to determine specific policy compliance regarding anonymity, plagiarism, or broader impact documentation, as no venue-specific policies or external overlap data are available. The paper does not contain a dedicated ethics or broader impact section, nor does it explicitly detail data licensing or consent procedures for the datasets used.","paper_id":"Byk-VI9eg","paper_identity_sha256":"71291ae735960ff5b3b03aad95893c9f588260a9aecba3781e80be857d922001","prompt_identity_sha256":"348167774054d243122297c86e850ec443188974d8ab4a4500aa874187ad80a1","raw_response_sha256":"64e7ef60fa01174a476921206d1b9c58bab6fa8860bfef79356e2c882f6aca2d","request_identity_sha256":"2b11fc0ecddd680439b8dc7699e854daa0ddfad9d77cd603ddfe23eeb67ff0c3","reviewer_identity_sha256":"32b29c26fbf1508e066dfb25b1a9a3fe0654c5869a7da3020e1e8e61940befe3","role":"POL","schema_version":"agentreview-full-review-corpus-v4","structural_context_sha256":"096273a068e928dc842304e951152e8ec4129b015fff65453efed98ff3693b30","subdimension_sections":[{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-021"],"review_text":"The paper does not include a dedicated section discussing ethical risks, fairness, bias, or potential harms associated with the generated images. While the work focuses on image generation using datasets like CelebA, which contains human faces, the text does not address issues of representation, privacy of the subjects in the training data, or the potential for misuse of the generated content. The absence of such discussion is noted as a limitation in the provided text.","subdimension_id":"POL-ETH"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-021"],"review_text":"The paper utilizes the MNIST, CIFAR-10, and CelebA datasets for evaluation. The text cites the original sources for these datasets but does not explicitly state the licensing terms, consent procedures, or privacy compliance measures adhered to during their use. Specifically, for the CelebA dataset, which involves images of celebrities, the paper does not provide evidence of consent or discuss how privacy regulations were respected. The supplied evidence is insufficient to determine full data usage and privacy compliance.","subdimension_id":"POL-DAT"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-001"],"review_text":"The paper explicitly lists the authors' names (Ishan Durugkar, Ian Gemp, Sridhar Mahadevan), their institutional affiliation (University of Massachusetts, Amherst), and their email addresses on the title page. While this is standard for published versions, it would violate double-blind review policies if this were a submission. However, without a frozen venue-specific anonymity policy for the review context, this is described as a visible identification of authors rather than a declared policy violation.","subdimension_id":"POL-ANO"},{"paper_anchor_ids":[],"review_text":"The supplied evidence does not contain information regarding plagiarism, self-plagiarism, or dual submission. There is no external overlap data or frozen plagiarism evidence available to assess the originality of the content or figures. Therefore, the supplied paper-only evidence is insufficient to determine the plagiarism or dual submission status.","subdimension_id":"POL-PLG"},{"paper_anchor_ids":[],"review_text":"The paper does not include a broader impact statement, a responsible AI checklist, or explicit documentation of IRB/ethics approvals. It also does not specify the software or data licenses used for the code or datasets beyond standard citations. Without a frozen policy obligation requiring these specific documents, the absence of these sections is noted, but the supplied evidence is insufficient to determine compliance with specific broader impact or societal consideration policies.","subdimension_id":"POL-IMP"}]},"disposition":"CANONICAL_FULL_REVIEW_COMMITTED","item_commit_sha256":"d9f98f6d4342173989ad044f5fb5acf8bb092f76ac2359d4d4a8a495f591241c","paper_id":"Byk-VI9eg","paper_ordinal":77,"raw_attempts":[{"assistant_content_base64":"","assistant_content_sha256":"64e7ef60fa01174a476921206d1b9c58bab6fa8860bfef79356e2c882f6aca2d","attempt_index":0,"error":"","finish_reason":"stop","paper_id":"Byk-VI9eg","raw_provider_response_base64":"","raw_provider_response_sha256":"ec4ac2ce1a726bb518d802256f044cbc51af30e5ba3f03696f1e1d4919539e95","request_identity_sha256":"2b11fc0ecddd680439b8dc7699e854daa0ddfad9d77cd603ddfe23eeb67ff0c3","role":"POL","schema_version":"no-memory-full-review-corpus-build-v6","usage":{"completion_tokens":745,"prompt_tokens":17059,"prompt_tokens_details":null,"total_tokens":17804},"valid":true}],"request_identity_sha256":"2b11fc0ecddd680439b8dc7699e854daa0ddfad9d77cd603ddfe23eeb67ff0c3","role":"POL","role_ordinal":4,"schema_version":"corpus-build-bootstrap-checkpoint-v4"}